# Bootstrap GitHub Actions OIDC for AWS – Implementation Complete ✅

## Problem Solved
GitHub Actions CI/CD requires AWS IAM credentials to deploy infrastructure. Using OIDC federation eliminates the need for static secrets, but it creates a **chicken-and-egg problem**: the role can't exist until the infrastructure stack is deployed, but the workflow can't run until the role exists.

## Solution Implemented
Created a **separate bootstrap layer** at `infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/` that:
- Creates the GitHub OIDC provider (account-level, one-time)
- Creates a minimal GitHub Actions IAM role
- Outputs the role ARN for use in workflows
- Can be applied locally before any workflows run

## Files Created

### Core Infrastructure Files

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/versions.tf`**
- Terraform version constraints (>= 1.5)
- AWS provider v5.0+
- TLS provider for certificate handling

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/main.tf`**
- Uses the reusable `../modules/github-oidc-role` module
- Creates GitHub OIDC provider (idempotent)
- Creates IAM role with strict trust policy
- Trust policy scoped to: `repo:owner/repo:ref:refs/heads/main`
- No inline or managed policies (lean design)

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/variables.tf`**
- `aws_region` – AWS region (default: us-east-1)
- `github_owner` – GitHub org/user
- `github_repo` – Repository name
- `github_subject_type` – "branch" or "environment"
- `github_subject_value` – Branch name or environment (default: main)
- `role_name` – IAM role name (account ID prefixed for uniqueness)
- `tags` – Common tags for all resources

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/outputs.tf`**
- `github_oidc_role_arn` – **Primary output for GitHub secrets**
- `github_oidc_role_name` – Role name for reference
- `github_oidc_provider_arn` – Provider ARN (account-level resource)
- `github_subject_claim` – Exact subject claim (for debugging)

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/terraform.tfvars.example`**
- Example configuration with your repository details
- Copy to `terraform.tfvars` and populate with GitHub repo info

### Documentation

**`infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/README.md`**
Comprehensive guide covering:
